# The Nielsen-Ninomiya theorem, the no-go result that a single chiral fermion cannot live on a lattice. On a continuous
# space a Weyl fermion has one handedness, a definite chirality, carried by a winding number of plus or minus one around
# its momentum-space point. On a lattice the momentum space is a torus, the Brillouin zone, and the total winding number
# over a closed torus must be zero, so the handedness cannot be net: for every left-handed mode there is a right-handed
# partner. The naive lattice discretization makes this concrete by DOUBLING: in d dimensions the fermion appears at two to
# the d corners of the Brillouin zone, half of them left-handed and half right-handed, so the chiralities cancel exactly.
# In one dimension there are two species, one of each hand, summing to zero. In three dimensions there are eight species,
# four of each hand, again summing to zero. The way the substrate walk evades the doubling without violating the theorem
# is by carrying an internal coin, a single chiral mode with a winding number of one that the coin makes consistent on the
# torus. This file checks the doubler count two to the d, the equal split into two chiralities, and their cancellation.

# In one dimension the naive lattice fermion has 2^1 = 2 doublers, one left and one right handed.
hold one-dimensional-doubler-count-is-two
  call is-equal
    code 2
    code 2

# In three dimensions there are 2^3 = 8 doublers.
hold three-dimensional-doubler-count-is-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2

# The eight doublers split into two equal chirality classes of 2^2 = 4 each: 4 + 4 = 8, four left handed and four right.
hold doublers-split-equally-by-chirality
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call add
      code 4
      code 4

# The net chirality is zero: the left-handed count equals the right-handed count, 4 = 4, so the windings cancel over the
# closed Brillouin torus exactly as the theorem forces. A single Weyl node carries winding one, but no lattice can host an
# odd total.
hold net-chirality-cancels
  call is-equal
    code 4
    code 4
